## Colors
- **Primary** (`{colors.primary}`): the single interactive accent. At most one filled primary button per view.
- **Surface / Surface raised**: page and raised-panel backgrounds. In dark mode, raised surfaces get lighter.
- **On-surface / On-surface muted**: text. Both ≥ 4.5:1 on every surface they sit on; aim for 7:1 on custom dark pairs.
- **Border / Border strong**: decorative hairline vs control boundary (≥ 3:1 where the boundary is needed to identify the control or its state, including checked vs unchecked).
- **Error / Success / Warning**: status only, always paired with an icon or text; never colour alone (must pass a grayscale check).
- **Theme**: follows the OS by default. If a switch exists: System (default) / Light / Dark. Every custom colour has light, dark, increased-contrast light and increased-contrast dark values: <list or "generated by …">.
- **Gradients**: none as decoration. <Allowed only as: an established brand asset, or the single AI-state indicator described in "AI states" — delete if not applicable.>
- Palette source: <OKLCH generator / brand book>. Dark theme: <how generated>.

## Typography
| Token | Size | Weight | Line height | Tracking | Use |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| display-lg | 48 | 600 | 1.1 | −0.03em | Marketing hero only |
| headline-lg | 30 | 600 | 1.2 | −0.02em | Page titles |
| headline-md | 24 | 600 | 1.25 | −0.015em | Section titles |
| title | 18 | 600 | 1.35 | 0 | Card/dialog titles |
| body-lg | 16 | 400 | 1.5 | 0 | Default body, inputs (16px avoids iOS input zoom) |
| body-md | 14 | 400 | 1.5 | 0 | Dense UI body |
| label-md / label-sm | 14 / 12 | 500 | 1.35 | 0 | Buttons, labels, meta |
| label-caps | 12 | 500 | 1.35 | +0.06em | Short uppercase labels only |
| numeric | 14 | 400 | 1.5 | 0 | Tables, prices, timers (`tnum`) |
| mono | 13 | 400 | 1.5 | 0 | Code, IDs |

Principles: ≤ 3 sizes in a simple view; weights 400/500/600 (never below 400 for UI text); tracking tightens as size grows (tune per font; don't copy SF Pro's table); body measure 45–75 characters (aim ~66; 40–60 on narrow columns); body line-height 1.4–1.6, tighter only for headings and labels; numerals in UI; case convention: <sentence case (web) | HIG title case for native Apple buttons, menus and section headers>. Type scales with `rem` and survives 200% text.
Font substitutes: <proprietary → open fallback>. Don't ship SF fonts or SF Symbols in a web app.

## Layout
- 4px base; only scale values (front matter `spacing`). Space inside a group < space between groups. Padding inside, `gap` between children.
- Container: <max width, e.g. 1200px>; app shell: <fixed sidebar + fluid content>; buttons, inputs and forms never stretch full width on wide screens.
- Breakpoints (layout follows available space, never device type; functionality is identical at every size):

| Name | Width | Key changes |
|---|---|---|
| compact | < 600 | single column; 16px margins; bottom actions use safe-area insets; bottom sheets instead of popovers |
| medium | 600–839 | 24px margins; nav rail or collapsible sidebar; 1 pane (2 only for low-density content) |
| expanded | 840–1199 | 2 panes, 24px gutter; visible primary nav (no hamburger) |
| large | ≥ 1200 | fixed side pane ~360–412px; up to 3 panes at ≥ 1600 |

- Touch targets ≥ 44×44 (48×48 on Material) on touch, ≥ 24×24 on pointer; hit area may exceed the visual. Mobile web baseline: `viewport-fit=cover`, never disable zoom, `100dvh` shells / `100svh` heroes, hover styles behind `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`.

## Elevation & Depth
| Level | Treatment | Use |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | flat; group with spacing | default |
| 1 | inset 1px `{colors.border}` ring, or `surface-raised` | cards, panels |
| 2 | ring + 2 stacked low-alpha shadows (tinted to surface hue) | popovers, menus |
| 3 | ring + 3 stacked shadows + scrim | dialogs, sheets |

### Shadow tokens
<!-- The spec has no shadow tokens; values live here. Mirror them as CSS custom properties. One light source (top), shadows tinted to the surface hue, never pure grey halos. -->
| Token | Value (light) | Use |
|---|---|---|
| shadow-1 | `0 1px 2px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.06)` | resting raised card (optional; prefer the ring) |
| shadow-2 | `0 1px 2px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.06), 0 4px 12px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.08)` | popovers, menus |
| shadow-3 | `0 2px 4px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.06), 0 8px 24px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.10), 0 24px 48px rgb(24 24 27 / 0.12)` | dialogs |
| scrim | `rgb(0 0 0 / 0.32)` | behind modal dialogs and sheets |

Dark mode: lighter surface steps + hairlines instead of shadows. Never border + heavy shadow + background shift together. Translucency (`backdrop-filter`) only on floating chrome, never glass on glass and never on content cards; solid under `prefers-reduced-transparency`, solid + outline under `prefers-contrast: more`.

## Shapes
Radius set: sm 4 · md 8 · lg 12 · xl 16 · full. Nested radius = outer − padding (concentric). One CTA radius grammar per screen (<pills | rounded rectangles>). No large or pill radii on dense data cards. Icons: <one family>, <stroke> stroke, sized to drawn size, weight matched to adjacent text; outline at rest, filled for selected; no emoji as icons; standard metaphors for share, search, delete; the ellipsis only for overflow.

## Components
For each component list: variants, sizes, and ALL states (default, hover, active/pressed, focus-visible, disabled-with-reason, loading, selected, error), plus the library or primitive it builds on. New state = new sibling key in the front matter (`-hover`, `-active`, `-disabled`).
- **Button**: primary (one per view) / secondary / tertiary (link-style) / destructive (styled destructive but never the Enter default; focus the least destructive option). Label = outcome verb + object. Loading keeps label width and blocks resubmit. Press `scale(0.97)`. Disabled buttons explain why and never use `pointer-events: none`.
- **Input**: persistent visible label above, hint below the label, error text tied to the field; ≥ 16px text on touch; correct `type`/`inputmode`/`autocomplete`/`enterkeyhint`. Validate on submit, then live once a field has errored.
- **Card**, **Dialog** (one layer at a time; dirty dialogs offer Save/Discard on every dismissal), **Menu/Popover** (from trigger origin; bottom sheet on compact), **Toast** (<library>; polite live region; actionable toasts don't auto-dismiss), **Table** (tabular numerals, sticky header, never truncate numbers), **Empty state** (what + why + next action).
- Library: <shadcn/ui | Radix | Base UI | platform components>.

## Do's and Don'ts
- Do use `{colors.primary}` only for the single most important action per view, links, selection and focus.
- Do build every data view's ideal, empty, loading, partial and error states, and test them with worst-case data.
- Do keep text ≥ 4.5:1 (3:1 only for ≥ 24px or ≥ 18.66px bold), identifying UI boundaries and focus ≥ 3:1, in light, dark and increased-contrast modes.
- Do give every gesture and hover action a visible control alternative.
- Don't add a second accent colour to chrome or put brand colour on every control.
- Don't use more than 3 font weights, or weights below 400 for UI text.
- Don't mix pill and rectangular buttons in one view.
- Don't use gradients, glow or glass as decoration or on content cards.
- Don't animate keyboard-initiated or 100+/day actions.

## Motion
| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| ease-out | cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1) | enter/exit (default) |
| ease-in-out | cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1) | on-screen movement, morphing |
| ease-drawer | cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1) | drawers/sheets |
| press | 160ms | `:active` scale 0.97 |
| micro | 100–200ms | hover colour, toggles, small state changes |
| tooltip | 125ms | after the first opens, instant |
| dropdown / popover | 150–250ms | from trigger origin, start at scale 0.95 + opacity 0 |
| modal | 200–250ms | centred, scale 0.96 |
| toast-enter | ~400ms | `ease`; exits faster |
| drawer / sheet | up to ~500ms | ease-drawer; large surfaces travelling far |

Rules: frequency gate (no animation for keyboard-initiated or 100+/day actions; reduce for tens/day); a stated purpose for every animation; transform and opacity only; never `scale(0)`; no `ease-in` on UI; exits faster than entrances; interruptible (transitions, not keyframes, for UI that can reverse); hover motion behind `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`. **Reduced motion**: remove decorative and ongoing motion (parallax, auto-advance, spin, animated blur); replace meaningful motion with a fade, highlight or colour change; never blanket-kill feedback. Key moments are documented as named phases with their parameters: <phase list>.

## Accessibility
- Target: WCAG 2.2 AA; on Apple platforms, the Accessibility Nutrition Label criteria (VoiceOver, Larger Text, Sufficient Contrast, Reduced Motion, Differentiate Without Color Alone) for every main task.
- Focus ring: 2px solid `{colors.primary}`, 2px offset, `outline` (survives forced colours); two-tone ring on varied surfaces. Focus never obscured by sticky UI; focus returns to the trigger on close; background loads never move focus or reading position.
- Keyboard map for composite widgets: <toolbar / tabs / menu / listbox / grid: arrow keys within, one tab stop>. Global shortcuts: <⌘K, /, ?, …>.
- Targets: 24px floor, 44/48px on touch; ~12px clear space around bezeled controls.
- Supported preferences (honour the OS; in-app settings only if more granular): reduced motion, reduced transparency, increased contrast (`prefers-contrast: more` adds borders), dark mode, forced colours, 200% text (layouts stack, rows grow, no truncation without a path to the full text).
- Accessible names: concise, item-specific for repeated or destructive actions ("Delete invoice 1042"), never include the role ("button") or state.
- Testing: main tasks × one setting at a time, then combinations (dark + increased contrast + reduced transparency); keyboard only; screen reader with the screen off; voice control; grayscale; axe in CI. Record pass/fail per task.

## Voice & Copy
Case: <sentence case | HIG title case on native Apple>. Buttons are outcome verb + object ("Save changes", not "Submit"). Errors say what happened + how to fix, with no "we", blame or "please": "Couldn't save changes. Check your connection and try again." Numerals in UI. Turn on/off, not enable/disable; no "click on", "e.g.", "Oops". Terminology (one name per concept): <noun list>. Fixture names are diverse and plausible; no lorem ipsum.

## AI states
<!-- Delete this section if the product has no AI features. -->
AI marker: <one icon> always paired with a verb label ("Summarise"). States and their single treatment: idle · listening · thinking (Stop) · streaming (Stop) · done (Copy, Retry, Edit, Undo, sources) · error (Retry, input kept) · cancelled (partial kept). Gradient/animated indicator: <none | describe; tied to a state, stops when it ends, static + text under reduced motion>. Generated changes are previewed and undoable; consequential actions confirmed.

## Iteration Guide
1. Change one component at a time; reference tokens by name (`{components.button-primary}`), never inline hex or px.
2. New state = new sibling component key (`-hover`, `-active`, `-disabled`).
3. Before adding chrome (border, shadow, colour), try spacing, then a surface step.
4. For open-ended work, explore 2–3 named directions before converging; record the rejected ones.
5. Update this file in the same change as the code; run the linter.

